        ],
        "finding": "After a successful dig, join copies the smaller endpoint label to the other endpoint. This inspected update does not relabel every room sharing the old label. Treat labels as construction bookkeeping; do not claim canonical disjoint-set components or runtime accessibility."
      },
      "scope": "Only downloaded source files were searched; whole-repository absence of other writes is not established."
    },
    "doorStateTrace": {
      "path": "src/mklev.c",
      "lines": [
        384,
        447
      ],
      "finding": "Door geometry has separate state: ordinary doors may be open, locked, closed or absent; secret doors are closed or locked. Difficulty and shop context affect traps, and some trapped-door branches can create a mimic. A successful corridor dig alone does not establish unimpeded movement."
    }
